# Utility XML to PDF
Utility XML to PDF V2

## Parameters
[Error Handling]
  Select between returning an error message, or raising an exception.
[Kapp Slug]
  The kapp to upload the file to.
[Form Slug]
  The form to upload the file to.
[Filename]
  The name to give the created file without the 'pdf' extension.

[Image Attachment Mappings]
  A JSON object that maps how attachments fields should be processed. This format is very specific, and does support attachments from multiple submissions:
  ```{
    "submission_id": {
      "signature_field": {
        "tag_pattern": "##Signature_*##",
        "image_template": "<img src=\"\" width=\"200\" class=\"signature\"></img>"
      },
      "photos_field": {
        "tag_pattern": "##Photo_*##",
        "image_template": "<img src=\"\" class=\"photo\"></img>"
      }
    }
  }```

  Note: If the tag_pattern is left off, the ##<attachment_field_name>_*## is used as the tag.
  Note: If the image_template is left off, '<img src="" width="600" height="auto"></img><br/>' is used.

[XHTML]
  Well formed XHTML input as string. Use the tag pattern(s) specified in the Attachment Mappings input (i.e., "##Signature_*##") to indicate where the image elements should appear.

## Results
[Handler Error Message]
  Error message if an error was encountered and Error Handling is set to "Error Message".
[File]
  The file reference to the uploaded file in the Kinetic Filestore

### Sample configuration
Error Handling:              Raise Error
Kapp Slug:                   services
Form Slug:                   pdf-signature-test
Filename:                    SignedDocument
Image Attachment Mappings:   {"4c31e018-fda9-11ec-8db2-e58d8bda3aca": {"Signature": {"tag_pattern":"##Image_*##", "image_template":"<img src=\"\" width=\"200\"></img>"}}},
XHTML:                       ```<html>
<head>
<style type="text/css">

style { display: none }
p { display: block; color: green }
p.note { color: red }
b {font-weight: bold }
hr {margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; border-top:1px solid black}

</style>
<title>Your Title Here</title>
</head>
<body>
<hr></hr>
<a href="http://somegreatsite.com=">Link Name</a>
is a link to another nifty site
<h1>This is a Header</h1>
<h2>This is a Medium Header</h2>
Send me mail at <a href="mailto:support@yourcompany.com">
support@yourcompany.com</a>.
<p> This is a new paragraph!</p>
<p> <b>This is a new paragraph!</b></p>
<p> <b>WAHOO!</b> </p>
<br></br>
<br></br>
<br></br>
<b><i>This is a new sentence without a paragraph break, in bold italics.</i></b>
<hr></hr>
##Image_*##"
</body>
</html>```

## Detailed Description
  This handler generates a PDF file based on inputs.  It can include an image attachments from an existing submissions.
  The PDF file is uploaded to the Kinetic Platform Filestore and the output is the reference to the file.  A second
  handler or routine (e.g., Kinetic Submission Update) should be used to update an attachment field with the output
  from this handler.

  Images will not process styling against the img tag or via CSS classes.  The way to control image sizing is to
  include a 'width' or 'height' property on the image element.  Without at least a width value, the image will be
  rendered in its intrinsic size.  When included, height and width are pixels (e.g., 200 equates to 200px).
